WEBVTT

00:01.570 --> 00:04.810
Mamoru... No!

00:04.810 --> 00:05.800
No!

00:07.290 --> 00:09.240
<i>I can’t forget...</i>

00:09.240 --> 00:11.760
<i>It isn’t me who’s hurt.</i>

00:12.540 --> 00:15.490
<i>It’s Ayako-san!</i>

00:25.840 --> 00:29.430
Ayako-san, I’ll protect you!

00:43.610 --> 00:45.710
Hurry up!

00:47.630 --> 00:49.070
What?

00:49.070 --> 00:51.700
That cry is different than the other ones it’s made.

01:20.430 --> 01:21.610
<i>Mamoru...</i>

01:24.490 --> 01:26.020
<i>It’s OK.</i>

01:26.020 --> 01:27.960
<i>I’m not going anywhere.</i>

01:28.600 --> 01:31.540
<i>I’ll be with you forever.</i>

01:32.540 --> 01:36.820
<i>No matter what happens...
We’ll be together forever... Forever.</i>

01:39.360 --> 01:41.330
I’m back, Mamoru.

01:41.330 --> 01:42.870
Ayako-san...

01:42.870 --> 01:47.250
Your heart saved me.

01:48.100 --> 01:51.780
You always protect me.

01:52.480 --> 01:57.500
Yes, if you’re with me, I’m invincible.

02:15.220 --> 02:18.570
Today’s the day we’re supposed to
get a message from Germany...

02:18.570 --> 02:20.240
so we came early, but...

02:20.660 --> 02:24.250
All of our toys went at once.

02:24.250 --> 02:25.190
Yeah.

02:25.880 --> 02:26.960
No good.

02:27.500 --> 02:29.340
This is no good!

02:29.340 --> 02:32.250
I should just disappear!

02:32.250 --> 02:34.990
What a pathetic man.

02:34.990 --> 02:36.670
Just knock her to the ground if you have to.

02:36.670 --> 02:39.610
I’ll get a shot of you saying goodbye to this life!

02:40.130 --> 02:41.770
I’m so excited!

02:41.770 --> 02:43.570
Oh, crazy for you!

02:44.440 --> 02:48.510
Hey, the flash is gonna reflect off the screen!

02:49.030 --> 02:52.110
Even without our toys, they’re still having fun.

02:52.110 --> 02:55.650
I can’t believe they all love soap operas...

02:55.650 --> 02:58.370
And a late night rebroadcast?

02:57.710 --> 03:02.490
We interrupt <i>The Great Murder World of Love</i> to bring you an emergency news bulletin.

02:58.370 --> 02:59.750
Youko, Anna!

02:59.750 --> 03:01.460
You changed the channel, didn’t you?

03:01.460 --> 03:03.160
I didn’t do anything.

03:03.760 --> 03:05.700
And now an emergency news bulletin.

03:05.700 --> 03:07.220
The United Nations have announced

03:07.220 --> 03:10.370
they have completed launch preparations
for that very dangerous thing.

03:08.000 --> 03:10.370
That

03:11.530 --> 03:15.150
Man, soap operas have the
most exaggerated plot twists.

03:15.150 --> 03:18.250
Launching “that” just because some
guy ditched you? Seriously?

03:18.250 --> 03:19.760
Bomb ahead!

03:19.760 --> 03:21.220
My hands are getting sweaty.

03:21.220 --> 03:25.060
Um, is this really part of the show?

03:25.060 --> 03:31.230
Ayako might do it, if she thought
Mamoru-san were cheating on her...

03:31.230 --> 03:33.500
She’d be like, “Boom!”

03:33.500 --> 03:37.970
The world’s nations have activated special article five of the Beatrice Charter.

03:39.440 --> 03:43.110
This is the center of the beatrice energy, taken by a long-range camera.

03:44.240 --> 03:46.890
You can see what appear to be humans inside,

03:46.890 --> 03:49.880
but experts say this is something the Beatrice Cluster

03:48.570 --> 03:50.990
Oh my, I didn’t think it was her.

03:49.880 --> 03:53.690
has created that just happens to appear human...

03:50.990 --> 03:53.690
It’s too easy to tell it’s Ayako-san!

04:01.560 --> 04:04.580
You were absorbed by the Return to the Beginning.

04:05.290 --> 04:10.970
The missiles are aimed at you.

04:11.740 --> 04:14.570
If I have Mamoru, I’m invincible.

04:15.530 --> 04:17.850
This isn’t the time for jokes!

04:17.850 --> 04:19.300
I’m serious.

04:19.300 --> 04:21.710
I’m invincible if I have Mamoru.

04:21.710 --> 04:23.130
Right, Mamoru?

04:23.130 --> 04:23.880
Yes.

04:23.880 --> 04:25.560
Don’t be stupid!

04:25.560 --> 04:27.880
Maria, Johan, help me!

04:28.340 --> 04:31.600
If the planet’s three greatest
beatrice users work together,

04:31.600 --> 04:32.780
then just maybe...

04:32.780 --> 04:34.290
No way.

04:35.050 --> 04:37.830
You can tell. Right, Johan?

04:37.830 --> 04:42.740
There are no gaps to enter their beatrice.

04:45.250 --> 04:50.380
Masaki, I’ll tell you what the beatrice’s thoughts were,

04:50.380 --> 04:52.510
while it was in the Return to the Beginning.

05:00.650 --> 05:02.860
The beatrice’s thoughts?

05:02.860 --> 05:05.070
When I was surrounded by it,

05:05.070 --> 05:07.450
I could feel it...

05:11.230 --> 05:15.070
The beatrice didn’t want to be united as one.

05:16.400 --> 05:20.540
It was afraid of becoming one.

05:20.540 --> 05:23.610
Sometimes power makes thought impossible.

05:24.280 --> 05:28.950
It was afraid of massive destructive
impulses that it couldn’t control.

05:29.810 --> 05:34.590
When it was forced to unite,
the beatrice chose me as its medium.

05:35.050 --> 05:36.690
Because it hoped...

05:38.180 --> 05:39.520
That I would destroy it.

05:41.390 --> 05:45.310
It hoped that I would destroy it.

05:46.110 --> 05:48.320
And that was...

05:55.260 --> 05:58.680
because I have Mamoru with me.

05:58.680 --> 05:59.640
Me?

06:02.180 --> 06:04.820
I was just like the beatrice.

06:05.670 --> 06:12.290
I was always afraid of becoming one,
of connecting with someone.

06:16.990 --> 06:17.760
Ayako...

06:17.760 --> 06:22.770
I was afraid of seeking someone and being left behind.

06:23.600 --> 06:27.360
I was afraid of the unending darkness within me,

06:27.360 --> 06:29.790
which was born when that happened.

06:30.410 --> 06:33.910
So I froze my heart.

06:36.860 --> 06:40.280
I wouldn’t let anyone...

06:44.300 --> 06:46.880
Anyone but myself deep inside.

06:51.170 --> 06:56.770
It was you, Mamoru, who shattered that frozen heart.

06:57.290 --> 06:58.700
Ayako-san...

07:01.140 --> 07:02.910
Your smile,

07:03.240 --> 07:05.210
your memories,

07:05.890 --> 07:07.740
your innocence,

07:08.430 --> 07:10.440
your kindness...

07:13.560 --> 07:17.470
All of your self destroyed my fear.

07:19.070 --> 07:23.310
I’m not scared of becoming one with someone anymore.

07:25.260 --> 07:34.240
Yes. The beatrice chose me because
it believed you would destroy it.

07:40.160 --> 07:44.480
Mamoru-kun amplifies the Witch Beatrice’s beatrice.

07:44.480 --> 07:47.030
I knew that,

07:47.030 --> 07:50.190
but I didn’t know that the
beatrice loved them that much.

07:50.680 --> 07:52.630
True love.

07:52.630 --> 07:53.620
Masaki?

07:54.160 --> 07:56.430
Mamoru-kun believed in the beatrice...

07:56.430 --> 07:59.860
and filled it with innocent love.

08:00.340 --> 08:02.300
And the beatrice...

08:02.870 --> 08:05.380
answered his feelings.

08:18.660 --> 08:20.390
Can you hear me, you two?

08:20.390 --> 08:23.980
The mid-range missiles are about to strike.

08:23.980 --> 08:27.390
There are eighty-six total,
seventy-two in the first round.

08:28.110 --> 08:33.870
Fifteen minutes later, the second,
long-range missiles will come.

08:33.870 --> 08:36.130
This should be obvious, but don’t miss any.

08:36.130 --> 08:38.770
Get them all in the stratosphere.

08:38.770 --> 08:40.510
Ayako-san, that’s what he said.

08:40.510 --> 08:41.960
Of course!

08:41.960 --> 08:43.960
Who does he think I am?

08:43.960 --> 08:46.540
Hey, I’m not done!

08:47.330 --> 08:49.450
Witch Beatrice, can you hear me?

08:50.340 --> 08:53.120
I still don’t believe it.

08:53.120 --> 08:57.530
I am the only one on this Earth worthy to be with you.

08:57.530 --> 09:00.690
That is an inescapable truth.

09:01.640 --> 09:03.170
Are you still...

09:03.170 --> 09:04.300
Then show me!

09:06.020 --> 09:07.770
I’m counting on you!

09:07.770 --> 09:09.030
Witch Beatrice!

09:09.030 --> 09:10.220
Ayako!

09:11.190 --> 09:15.900
Show me that your power is enough
to break this truth into a million pieces.

09:15.900 --> 09:17.980
Show me the power of your invincible love!

09:29.060 --> 09:30.010
They’re coming.

09:30.010 --> 09:31.430
Twelve o’clock, dead ahead.

09:40.250 --> 09:42.890
Next, ten o’clock to eight o’clock!

10:10.570 --> 10:11.990
You idiots!

10:11.990 --> 10:14.000
You guys are idiots!

10:14.370 --> 10:20.100
Why are you trying to end a fight
that we adults started?!

10:23.300 --> 10:24.430
Idiots...

10:24.430 --> 10:26.240
You guys are too amazing...

10:26.890 --> 10:30.200
We’re fools for not putting an end to this ourselves.

10:32.390 --> 10:34.420
This is the last round, Ayako-san.

10:35.000 --> 10:36.180
I know.

10:40.420 --> 10:41.510
Mamoru...

10:41.510 --> 10:42.060
Yeah?

10:43.000 --> 10:45.240
I love you, more than anyone.

10:46.450 --> 10:47.550
Yeah.

10:47.550 --> 10:50.430
I love you, too.

10:51.380 --> 10:52.700
I love you...

10:54.900 --> 10:56.660
I love you, Mamoru.

11:00.460 --> 11:01.730
I love you.

11:41.200 --> 11:47.690
Um... The necessary conditions to gather beatrice...

11:48.190 --> 11:50.980
Oh, you’re studying in the morning!

11:50.980 --> 11:52.730
That’s rare!

11:52.730 --> 11:54.620
You should at least knock!

11:55.680 --> 11:58.130
I made breakfast this morning.

11:58.130 --> 11:59.330
Come down.

11:59.330 --> 12:00.300
Right...

12:10.830 --> 12:15.660
<i>I hope I can come at least a little close
to Mamoru and Ayako-san.</i>

12:19.790 --> 12:24.230
Shizue
Yoshimura Mamoru

12:20.260 --> 12:22.140
Thank you!

12:27.610 --> 12:29.320
How’s the new kid?

12:29.320 --> 12:32.450
Said they had their own research..

12:34.110 --> 12:39.010
Jeez... Even Tsune’s better.

12:42.470 --> 12:43.560
This is...

12:45.840 --> 12:47.340
What are you doing?!

12:49.150 --> 12:51.780
More stupid research?

12:51.780 --> 12:54.870
You’ve got real work to do.

12:54.540 --> 12:56.460
Using Beatrice to Create a Safe Play Environment
for Young Children

12:54.870 --> 12:57.870
Get started.

12:57.870 --> 12:58.810
Listen!

12:58.810 --> 13:01.310
I haven’t given into you.

13:03.520 --> 13:08.470
I need to reevaluate my understanding of beatrice...

13:09.140 --> 13:12.940
If you’re that rebellious, I’ll punish you again.

13:14.490 --> 13:16.360
Punishment? What kind?

13:16.360 --> 13:18.960
They say that...
<i>Whisper whisper whisper.</i>

13:19.970 --> 13:21.900
How crazy...

13:21.900 --> 13:23.110
It’d give you a nosebleed!

13:24.920 --> 13:26.660
OK, thanks.

13:30.010 --> 13:33.490
You stupid crone!

13:34.660 --> 13:36.270
You guys get lost, too!

13:41.480 --> 13:44.130
It’s thanks to them...

13:52.180 --> 13:53.970
Witch Beatrice...

13:57.880 --> 14:00.960
We have lost two of our heroes.

14:01.580 --> 14:04.780
But does this mean we have lost?

14:04.780 --> 14:05.700
No!

14:05.700 --> 14:06.990
It is a beginning!

14:07.420 --> 14:12.210
The beatrice strength of our school is less than 1/30th of what it was before.

14:12.650 --> 14:16.920
And yet, how have we managed
to carry on our studies this far?

14:17.390 --> 14:22.420
Everyone, the goal of the East-B
Student Council is justice!

14:26.130 --> 14:30.500
The Takasu Ayako and Yoshimura Mamoru
you loved have died!

14:31.570 --> 14:32.630
Why?!

14:37.680 --> 14:37.730
Food

14:37.690 --> 14:40.230
Food

14:38.430 --> 14:40.230
Because he’s a stupid kid.

14:40.710 --> 14:44.780
Next week, <i>The Blessings of Maria upon Tsune</i> begins.

14:43.940 --> 14:46.050
This is a lie

14:44.780 --> 14:46.030
Look forward to it...

14:46.030 --> 14:46.860
From the Witch Beatrice with Love

14:46.860 --> 14:48.330
Ow!

14:49.700 --> 14:51.770
Hey!

14:51.770 --> 14:55.480
What were you doing while we were gone?!

14:55.480 --> 14:57.950
Yeah, this is a bit too much...

15:03.800 --> 15:07.340
They made us go to some lab and spend
two weeks on a medical check,

15:07.340 --> 15:09.420
and then this is what we get when we return?

15:09.420 --> 15:12.300
Well, I heard you’d be coming out tomorrow.

15:12.300 --> 15:13.630
Dang it.

15:13.630 --> 15:17.020
Well, today’s the graduation ceremony.

15:17.020 --> 15:20.640
I wanted to see you and Yuuka on your last day.

15:30.550 --> 15:31.720
Welcome back!

15:31.720 --> 15:32.750
Amazing!

15:32.750 --> 15:33.940
I shall return!

15:33.940 --> 15:35.330
Hey, you two!

15:35.330 --> 15:36.530
Here we go!

15:36.530 --> 15:38.020
Take a pose!

15:41.850 --> 15:44.080
OK, open sesame!

15:46.960 --> 15:47.920
This is...

15:47.920 --> 15:49.670
Hey, you guys!

15:51.850 --> 15:52.950
I can fly!

15:52.950 --> 15:54.540
OK, nice shot!

15:54.540 --> 16:03.250
Graduation Speech

15:55.130 --> 15:59.720
Diplomas will be presented by
the graduating class representative.

15:59.720 --> 16:03.230
A senior in informatics, Sudou Maya.

16:03.570 --> 16:04.480
Here.

16:05.300 --> 16:06.580
Lovely.

16:07.960 --> 16:09.990
What is it, Emelenzia?

16:09.990 --> 16:13.910
I’m going to give up on being your girlfriend.

16:15.430 --> 16:17.010
Emelenzia...

16:17.010 --> 16:19.050
After seeing you two in Germany,

16:19.050 --> 16:22.570
I can’t imagine beating the Witch Beatrice.

16:22.570 --> 16:25.170
I’m not that stupid.

16:25.170 --> 16:26.390
Emelenzia...

16:26.390 --> 16:27.040
Um...

16:27.040 --> 16:29.460
So I’m going to give up!

16:34.880 --> 16:37.810
Celebrate Graduation

16:37.810 --> 16:40.690
We’re almost ready.

16:40.690 --> 16:44.960
So all that’s left is to call the
Student Council President and Yuuka-san.

16:44.960 --> 16:47.600
Ayako, we’re going.

16:47.600 --> 16:50.780
I’ll stay here and wait.

16:51.040 --> 16:52.950
Is there something going on?

16:54.020 --> 16:56.470
I forgot something important.

16:56.470 --> 16:59.350
Then, let’s go!

17:05.560 --> 17:07.480
Come out, Maya.

17:08.650 --> 17:10.820
I was going to say goodbye

17:10.820 --> 17:12.990
to the Student Council room
I spent so many hours in.

17:16.430 --> 17:17.500
Ayako...

17:17.500 --> 17:18.660
Maya.

17:19.660 --> 17:22.390
There’s something I always wanted to say.

17:22.390 --> 17:23.920
Ayako...

17:26.090 --> 17:32.170
I never thought of you as a friend or companion.

17:35.100 --> 17:37.030
I didn’t want to.

17:38.230 --> 17:43.370
I thought the minute I admitted you mattered to me,

17:44.570 --> 17:46.550
you’d vanish.

17:47.450 --> 17:49.330
But it’s different now.

17:51.810 --> 17:54.030
Mamoru-kun, right?

17:55.160 --> 17:57.760
Mamoru-kun let you believe...

17:59.510 --> 18:03.900
That there’s something that wouldn’t go anywhere, that wouldn’t break.

18:12.690 --> 18:13.640
What’s wrong?

18:13.640 --> 18:16.180
I don’t want to graduate.

18:16.730 --> 18:18.870
I don’t want to graduate...

18:21.060 --> 18:22.580
Don’t be a little kid.

18:22.580 --> 18:23.990
Shut up.

18:27.050 --> 18:28.950
Don’t tell them, OK?

18:28.950 --> 18:30.770
Right, got it.

18:30.770 --> 18:33.350
I’m going to keep counting on you.

18:33.350 --> 18:34.360
Yeah, from now on.

18:37.100 --> 18:39.520
Recording complete. No noise.

18:39.520 --> 18:41.220
There we go! She said we were friends!

18:41.220 --> 18:43.330
Friendship forever!

18:43.330 --> 18:49.160
Ayako... So that’s how you felt about us.

18:49.160 --> 18:53.150
Friendship... A word almost as slippery as love.

18:53.150 --> 18:55.090
Wh-Wh-Wh—

18:55.990 --> 18:58.850
Weren’t you giving up on Mamoru?

18:58.850 --> 19:04.030
Jirou and Saburou just taught me the word <i>l’amant</i>.

19:04.030 --> 19:05.630
L’amant?

19:05.630 --> 19:09.030
I am a woman of the shadows. I stay out of sight...

19:09.030 --> 19:12.170
You’re right in front of me!

19:12.170 --> 19:16.280
We’re all friends. You can forgive her for that.

19:16.900 --> 19:18.880
What?!

19:18.880 --> 19:22.890
I’ll bury you all in the darkness!

19:23.810 --> 19:25.210
Ouch!

19:25.210 --> 19:26.940
You’re not getting the tape back!

19:26.940 --> 19:28.940
This is really bad!

19:28.940 --> 19:30.270
R-Run!

19:30.270 --> 19:30.770
Right!

19:34.930 --> 19:37.530
Today’s a great day!

19:38.730 --> 19:41.210
I made a special one for you, Em-chan.

19:41.210 --> 19:43.580
I’m glad the size matches.

19:43.580 --> 19:44.600
Danke.

19:52.200 --> 19:55.200
That was quite the graduation ceremony, wasn’t it?

19:55.200 --> 19:57.810
It’s thanks to all you guys.

19:57.810 --> 20:00.970
The Witch Beatrice showed up
for the first time in a while, too.

20:00.970 --> 20:02.110
What?

20:02.110 --> 20:02.990
No.

20:05.740 --> 20:08.660
Ayako-san isn’t a witch.

20:08.660 --> 20:10.720
Um, well...

20:12.590 --> 20:13.810
She’s a goddess!

20:16.520 --> 20:19.070
Oh, M-Mamoru...

20:20.080 --> 20:22.910
It’s true, though.

20:22.910 --> 20:24.530
How silly.

20:36.060 --> 20:38.080
It reminds you, doesn’t it?

20:40.020 --> 20:43.590
Those cherry blossoms from the first time we met...

20:44.170 --> 20:47.890
I made them blossom with beatrice then, but...

20:49.790 --> 20:52.020
They were very pretty.

20:52.020 --> 20:56.610
No, these are far prettier.

20:58.460 --> 21:02.310
I suffered a lot because of the beatrice,

21:02.310 --> 21:07.030
but in some ways, I was relying on it.

21:08.290 --> 21:09.490
Ayako-san...

21:10.310 --> 21:12.890
The beatrice will solve it...

21:13.340 --> 21:15.990
No matter what it is, they’ll solve it by force.

21:15.990 --> 21:17.310
But...

21:18.950 --> 21:21.010
When I met you,

21:21.010 --> 21:25.770
I learned what it was to grow up naturally,
without relying on the beatrice.

21:27.990 --> 21:31.400
For spring to come naturally, for warmth to come...

21:32.290 --> 21:36.910
And these blooming cherry blossoms, these feelings...

21:38.800 --> 21:41.280
I love the beatrice.

21:44.410 --> 21:50.500
You lived in harmony with it,
and that’s how you became who you are.

21:50.500 --> 21:56.000
I always admired it, so I came to this school and met you.

21:56.390 --> 21:59.520
I’m thankful that I was able to see
these cherry blossoms with you.

21:59.520 --> 22:01.960
I’m thankful for everything.

22:02.430 --> 22:03.740
Mamoru...

22:09.370 --> 22:10.370
Stay still.

22:12.450 --> 22:14.530
Got it!

22:17.100 --> 22:18.470
Jeez...

22:20.050 --> 22:23.200
Your smile really is wonderful.

22:24.000 --> 22:25.240
Hey.

22:27.110 --> 22:29.200
How long are you going to stay there flirting?

22:29.200 --> 22:31.570
Love is forever!

22:33.240 --> 22:35.310
Got a shot of all the cherry blossoms in full bloom!

22:35.840 --> 22:37.890
If you don’t hurry, we’ll leave you behind.

22:37.890 --> 22:40.130
We’re meeting up at your house for the party.

22:40.130 --> 22:42.530
Hurry, hurry!

22:42.530 --> 22:44.480
Witch Beatrice... Mamoru!

22:44.480 --> 22:47.820
OK, let’s run to the sea.

22:47.820 --> 22:50.120
What?

22:50.120 --> 22:53.030
It seems like a good way to end the last episode, right?

22:53.030 --> 22:54.270
Ready, go!

22:54.270 --> 22:56.880
Last person has to buy everyone juice!

22:58.230 --> 22:59.880
Brother!

23:01.180 --> 23:02.740
Try and catch me!
